WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.028 --> 00:00:16.476
"Wow, training was intense."

2
00:00:17.576 --> 00:00:21.278
Brody collapsed onto a bench in Markos' courtyard that evening.

3
00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:23.899
Every muscle in his body ached.

4
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.181
"You did well, Brody."

5
00:00:26.881 --> 00:00:28.182
Markos sat beside him.

6
00:00:28.202 --> 00:00:32.124
"Hermes seemed pleased with your speed by the end of the session.

7
00:00:32.924 --> 00:00:34.865
And your long jump was much improved."

8
00:00:35.886 --> 00:00:38.247
"But not improved enough," Julia said.

9
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:41.029
"Did you see Athena's champion?

10
00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:43.490
He jumped much farther than you, Brody."

11
00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:49.734
"Julia!" At that moment Markos' older sister hurried toward Julia.

12
00:00:49.754 --> 00:00:52.235
"We need your help in the kitchen.

13
00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:53.716
The men are hungry."

14
00:00:53.736 --> 00:00:55.977
"That's right."

15
00:00:56.497 --> 00:00:57.898
Brody smirked at Julia.

16
00:00:57.918 --> 00:00:59.059
"We're hungry.

17
00:00:59.479 --> 00:01:01.020
Go cook our food, woman."

18
00:01:02.692 --> 00:01:04.032
Julia gritted her teeth.

19
00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:07.013
"I'm busy," she told Helene.

20
00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.674
"I'll be there in a minute."

21
00:01:10.514 --> 00:01:11.474
Helene frowned.

22
00:01:11.494 --> 00:01:12.935
"Please hurry.

23
00:01:13.995 --> 00:01:19.877
We're expecting Hermes and Caerus for dinner again, and Father wants them to be pleased with our hospitality."

24
00:01:19.897 --> 00:01:25.218
"You should go to the kitchen," Markos said to Julia as Helene disappeared.

25
00:01:25.238 --> 00:01:28.979
"Hermes will be angry if you are not following the customs here."

26
00:01:28.999 --> 00:01:32.340
"I'm going," Julia retorted.

27
00:01:33.164 --> 00:01:35.246
"But first we should talk about what to do."

28
00:01:35.266 --> 00:01:37.347
"What do you mean?"

29
00:01:37.907 --> 00:01:38.728
Brody asked.

30
00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:41.350
"We already know what we're going to do.

31
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:46.233
I'm going to keep training until I'm stronger and faster than I already am.

32
00:01:47.194 --> 00:01:52.217
Then, after I win the Olympics, we'll go on my victory tour before going home."

33
00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:55.779
"Forget your victory tour," Julia said.

34
00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:59.202
"The passage could close at any moment, remember?

35
00:02:00.503 --> 00:02:02.184
We need to get home as soon as we can."

36
00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:04.696
Brody shrugged.

37
00:02:05.176 --> 00:02:06.577
Julia worried too much.

38
00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:10.958
Hermes was a god, which meant Hermes could do anything.

39
00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:15.839
That probably included opening a new passage if the first one closed.

40
00:02:21.121 --> 00:02:25.122
Still, Brody was too tired to argue with Julia about it right now.

41
00:02:25.142 --> 00:02:27.722
"Okay," he agreed.

42
00:02:27.742 --> 00:02:32.464
"So the plan is, I win the Olympics, and then we go home.

43
00:02:32.644 --> 00:02:33.244
Is that better?"

44
00:02:35.284 --> 00:02:36.785
"Yes," she replied.

45
00:02:36.805 --> 00:02:40.427
"Julia!" Helene yelled again.

46
00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.348
Julia sighed loudly.

47
00:02:43.368 --> 00:02:47.030
"Coming!" she yelled back.

48
00:02:47.631 --> 00:02:49.492
Then she stomped off into the house.

49
00:02:51.153 --> 00:02:54.894
"She might be right, you know," Markos said after Julia was gone.

50
00:02:55.995 --> 00:02:59.777
"Once the Games are over, you should take the first opportunity to return home."

51
00:02:59.797 --> 00:03:04.880
"Why?" Brody stretched and yawned.

52
00:03:08.615 --> 00:03:09.976
He wondered what was for dinner.

53
00:03:09.996 --> 00:03:17.081
"Because Markos hesitated, glancing around carefully, and then lowered his voice.

54
00:03:17.101 --> 00:03:19.843
"The gods can't be trusted.

55
00:03:20.663 --> 00:03:23.946
If you delay, Hermes might forget his promise to let you go."

56
00:03:23.966 --> 00:03:27.969
"Really?" Brody blinked in surprise.

57
00:03:27.989 --> 00:03:32.052
"But don't worry too much," Markos said.

58
00:03:32.928 --> 00:03:37.190
"If you bring glory to Hermes through your performance in the Games, he might not forget.

59
00:03:38.311 --> 00:03:45.055
In fact, if you beat Zeus' champion, Hermes will probably let you do anything you want, including leave."

60
00:03:46.456 --> 00:03:47.656
Brody relaxed again.

61
00:03:47.676 --> 00:03:50.858
"Then I'll just have to win," he said.

62
00:03:50.878 --> 00:03:52.299
"No problem."

63
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:58.943
Over the next couple of days, Brody did his best to put the plan into action.

64
00:03:59.703 --> 00:04:03.774
He trained as hard as he could, doing everything Hermes asked him to do.

65
00:04:04.874 --> 00:04:10.799
Hermes was still focused on the running races in the Games, though he also made Brody practice wrestling

66
00:04:10.999 --> 00:04:12.180
and javelin throwing.

67
00:04:13.681 --> 00:04:18.344
Then one day Hermes told Brody it was time to practice throwing the discus.

68
00:04:20.446 --> 00:04:21.927
Brody had never done that before.

69
00:04:21.947 --> 00:04:26.110
"I'm really good at throwing a football," he told himself.

70
00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.572
"It's probably the same thing."

71
00:04:30.096 --> 00:04:34.357
But Brody quickly learned that a discus was a lot heavier than a football.

72
00:04:36.478 --> 00:04:41.399
His first few throws were a disaster; the discus landed near his feet with a thud.

73
00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:48.041
"This is definitely not going well," he thought, casting a look at Hermes.

74
00:04:51.182 --> 00:04:56.484
When Markos brought him some water, Brody stood watching Artemis' champion for a few minutes.

75
00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.661
The other athlete was nearby, practicing his discus throw too.

76
00:05:02.681 --> 00:05:05.082
"I get it!"

77
00:05:05.582 --> 00:05:06.802
Brody declared suddenly.

78
00:05:08.323 --> 00:05:12.004
The other athlete swung the discus a few times before releasing it.

79
00:05:12.024 --> 00:05:18.185
"Here." Brody thrust the water back at Markos and then grabbed the discus again.

80
00:05:19.606 --> 00:05:25.687
This time he swung the discus back and forth before throwing it, just like the other athlete had

81
00:05:25.727 --> 00:05:27.708
done. "Excellent!"

82
00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.682
Hermes cried as the discus flew halfway down the marked course.

83
00:05:33.043 --> 00:05:34.544
"Much better, my champion!

84
00:05:34.904 --> 00:05:35.944
Now try it again!"

85
00:05:37.445 --> 00:05:40.026
An hour later Brody's arm muscles were aching.

86
00:05:41.327 --> 00:05:43.068
But Hermes was beaming.

87
00:05:43.088 --> 00:05:45.870
"We're making progress, young mortal friend!

88
00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.772
We might just turn you into an Olympic champion yet.

89
00:05:51.332 --> 00:05:54.354
As soon as you've mastered the discus, we'll move on to boxing.

90
00:05:55.635 --> 00:05:57.476
Oh, and the chariot race, of course."

91
00:05:59.212 --> 00:06:00.072
"Chariot race?"

92
00:06:00.532 --> 00:06:01.333
Brody echoed.

93
00:06:01.353 --> 00:06:03.313
"You mean with horses?"

94
00:06:03.333 --> 00:06:05.114
"Of course."

95
00:06:05.974 --> 00:06:07.875
Hermes tapped his chin thoughtfully.

96
00:06:07.895 --> 00:06:14.116
"Poseidon owes me a favor—perhaps I'll ask him if I can borrow a team of horses."

97
00:06:16.057 --> 00:06:17.237
Brody was surprised.

98
00:06:18.018 --> 00:06:19.638
He didn't know much about horses.

99
00:06:21.559 --> 00:06:22.519
But he wasn't worried.

100
00:06:22.539 --> 00:06:26.200
"I've done great at everything else so far," he thought.

101
00:06:27.768 --> 00:06:30.250
"I'm sure I'll be great at chariot driving too!"

102
00:06:32.212 --> 00:06:35.735
Just then Apollo hurried over with Artemis at his heels.

103
00:06:37.537 --> 00:06:40.379
"You look happy, Hermes," Apollo declared.

104
00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:46.564
"I suppose that means you haven't heard the latest gossip about Zeus' champion."

105
00:06:46.584 --> 00:06:51.428
"Gossip doesn't worry me, my friend," Hermes retorted.

106
00:06:51.448 --> 00:06:55.452
"Not when I have the finest champion in Olympia."

107
00:06:57.288 --> 00:06:58.789
Brody grinned proudly.

108
00:06:58.809 --> 00:07:03.291
"The gossip should worry you," Artemis said.

109
00:07:03.311 --> 00:07:12.374
"Zeus claims that the mighty Alcides is training by racing against the swiftest deer in the forest—and beating

110
00:07:12.414 --> 00:07:13.475
them every time!"

111
00:07:13.495 --> 00:07:17.677
"That's right," Apollo added.

112
00:07:17.697 --> 00:07:25.520
"I hear that Alcides chases down wild boars and strangles them with his bare hands for his dinner.

113
00:07:28.048 --> 00:07:33.071
And he once threw the javelin so far that Zeus himself couldn't see where it landed."

114
00:07:34.992 --> 00:07:36.013
Hermes scoffed.

115
00:07:36.033 --> 00:07:40.235
"It's easy for Zeus to brag when nobody has seen his champion yet.

116
00:07:41.376 --> 00:07:45.578
I'll believe Zeus' tales when I finally see Alcides with my own eyes."

117
00:07:47.219 --> 00:07:54.223
After Apollo and Artemis left to share their gossip with Ares, Hermes looked less cheerful than he had

118
00:07:54.243 --> 00:07:55.124
a few minutes earlier.

119
00:07:56.556 --> 00:07:59.241
"Blast Zeus and his bragging," he muttered.

120
00:08:00.143 --> 00:08:01.325
He glanced at Brody.

121
00:08:01.345 --> 00:08:04.391
"But perhaps some of his tales are true.

122
00:08:05.172 --> 00:08:06.995
So you'd better keep training hard, boy!"
